findings.issue:
FP-0119 security review 1 notes 3 to 5 have no owner:
- the test-only work counter is only a proxy for CPU work;
- no case measures the peak allocation of a decode that fills the 65536-point budget;
- hostile-input containment rests on deterministic prefix and substitution tests in a Debug build, with no fuzzer and no ReleaseSafe or ReleaseFast run.
The review rates them notes, and FP-0119 is still active.
